> [The] main port of the Ionian[ League],[ and] leader of the revolt[ against] the Pers[ians (500]BC[),] Mile[tus lies on the] north[ bank] of the Me[ander] and some of the[ site] is under water for[ part] of the[ year.] The port,[ once] guarded by stone lions, is still visible[.] The extensive baths[ of] Faustina[, wife of Marcus] Aurel[ius], are[ said to] be the inspiration for the Turkish hamam[.]
A Byzantine[ castle, above] the large[ theatre], and a Seljuk carav[ans]arai are records[ of the town’s continual use, as is] the İlyas Bey Mosque (1403), constructed with coloured marble from the Roman buildings and with a beautifully carved mihrab. A superbly illustrated study has been published.
Dolmuş[ from S]öke drops off at the[ end] of a track 1km from the site.[]

